# validate reports a malformed value, an unknown key or a value of the wrong
# kind with the file, line and field, and lists every missing field and an
# unknown customer_id in the same run.
exits 1 invox validate -i fields.yaml
! stdout .
scrubpaths stderr got.txt
cmp got.txt want-fields.txt

# Unknown keys, removed keys and wrong kinds, in every file at once.
exits 1 invox validate -i unknown.yaml -c customers-unknown.yaml -u issuer-unknown.yaml
! stdout .
scrubpaths stderr got.txt
cmp got.txt want-unknown.txt

# A key whose value defines an anchor holds a definition for aliases, so it
# is not an unknown key.
exec invox validate -i anchors.yaml
! stdout .
cmp stderr want-anchors.txt

# A numeric customer_id is the customer's ID, not a missing value (#17).
exec invox validate -i numeric-id.yaml
! stdout .
cmp stderr want-numeric-id.txt

# A mapping where text belongs is an error, never "map[first:Appsters]" (#17).
exits 1 invox validate -i numeric-id.yaml -c customers-mapping-name.yaml
! stdout .
scrubpaths stderr got.txt
cmp got.txt want-mapping-name.txt

# A problem in another customer's entry does not stop this invoice.
exec invox validate -i numeric-id.yaml -c customers-mapping-name-other.yaml
! stdout .
cmp stderr want-numeric-id.txt

-- fields.yaml --
customer_id: NOPE-1
invoice:
  number: NOPE-1-001
  issue_date: 2026-03-06
positions:
  - name: Development
    unit_price: 10
    quantity: 0
-- want-fields.txt --
error: fields.yaml: unknown customer_id `NOPE-1`
invoice.due_date: missing value
invoice.period: missing value
positions[1].description: missing value
positions[1].quantity: must be > 0
invoice.vat_percent: missing value
Run 'invox customer list' to see the customer IDs.
-- unknown.yaml --
customer_id: CUST-001
line_items: []
invoice:
  number: CUST-001-001
  issue_date: 2026-03-06
  due_date: 2026-04-05
  period: March
  vat_rate_percent: 20
  notes: call first
positions:
  - name: Development
    description: [Sprint, work]
    unit_price: 100
    quantity: 1
  - just a string
-- customers-unknown.yaml --
CUST-001:
  name: Appsters GmbH
  email: office@appsters.example
  phone: "+43 1 234"
  address:
    street: Hauptstrasse 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
    floor: 3
  tax:
    vat_tax_id: ATU12345678
-- issuer-unknown.yaml --
company: Boris Consulting
payment:
  bank_name: Test Bank
  iban: AT611904300234573201
  bic: BKAUATWW
  due_days: thirty
  payment_terms_text: Pay within 30 days
-- want-unknown.txt --
error: customers-unknown.yaml:4: unknown key "phone" in customer
customers-unknown.yaml:10: unknown key "floor" in customer.address
issuer-unknown.yaml:1: issuer.company must be a mapping, got a string
issuer-unknown.yaml:6: issuer.payment.due_days: expected an integer, got `thirty`
unknown.yaml:2: line_items: unsupported key; use positions
unknown.yaml:8: invoice.vat_rate_percent: unsupported key; use invoice.vat_percent
unknown.yaml:9: unknown key "notes" in invoice
unknown.yaml:12: positions[1].description: expected a string, got a list
unknown.yaml:15: positions[2] must be a mapping, got a string
invoice.vat_percent: missing value
Remove the unknown keys or fix their spelling; 'invox help customers' or 'invox help defaults' lists the supported fields.
-- anchors.yaml --
customer_id: CUST-001
reduced: &reduced
  vat_percent: 10
invoice:
  number: CUST-001-001
  issue_date: 2026-03-06
  due_date: 2026-04-05
  period: March
  vat_percent: 20
positions:
  - name: Development
    description: Sprint work
    unit_price: 100
    quantity: 2
  - <<: *reduced
    name: Book
    description: Reference
    unit_price: 10
    quantity: 1
-- want-anchors.txt --
Validation OK: CUST-001-001 for CUST-001, 2 line item(s), total 251,00 €
-- numeric-id.yaml --
customer_id: 1001
invoice:
  number: 1001-001
  issue_date: 2026-03-06
  due_date: 2026-04-05
  period: March
  vat_percent: 20
positions:
  - name: Development
    description: Sprint work
    unit_price: 100
    quantity: 1
-- want-numeric-id.txt --
Validation OK: 1001-001 for 1001, 1 line item(s), total 120,00 €
-- customers-mapping-name.yaml --
1001:
  name: {first: Appsters}
  email: office@appsters.example
  address:
    street: Hauptstrasse 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
  tax:
    vat_tax_id: ATU12345678
-- want-mapping-name.txt --
error: customers-mapping-name.yaml:2: customer.name: expected a string, got a mapping
-- customers-mapping-name-other.yaml --
1001:
  name: Appsters GmbH
  email: office@appsters.example
  address:
    street: Hauptstrasse 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
  tax:
    vat_tax_id: ATU12345678
2002:
  name: {first: Other}
  phone: unknown key in another customer
-- home/.config/invox/config.yaml --
archive:
  dir: archive
-- home/.config/invox/customers.yaml --
1001:
  name: Numeric GmbH
  email: numeric@example.com
  address:
    street: Zahlenweg 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
  tax:
    vat_tax_id: ATU11111111
CUST-001:
  name: Appsters GmbH
  status: active
  email: office@appsters.example
  email_greeting: Dear Jane Doe,
  contact_person: Jane Doe
  address:
    street: Hauptstrasse 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
  tax:
    vat_tax_id: ATU12345678
  billing:
    currency: EUR
CUST-002:
  name: Second Customer OG
  status: inactive
  email: billing@second.example
  address:
    street: Nebenstrasse 2
    postal_code: "8010"
    city: Graz
    country: Austria
CUST-003:
  name: Third Customer KG
  status: active
  email: billing@third.example
  address:
    street: Seeweg 3
    postal_code: "5020"
    city: Salzburg
    country: Austria
-- home/.config/invox/issuer.yaml --
company:
  legal_company_name: Boris Consulting
  company_registration_number: FN 123456a
  vat_tax_id: ATU87654321
  website: https://example.com
  email: hello@example.com
  address:
    street: Ring 1
    postal_code: "1010"
    city: Vienna
    country: Austria
payment:
  bank_name: Test Bank
  iban: AT611904300234573201
  bic: BKAUATWW
  due_days: 30
  payment_terms_text: Pay within 30 days
-- home/.config/invox/invoice_defaults.yaml --
invoice:
  period: "Leistungszeitraum: "
  vat_percent: 20
  paid_amount: 0
positions:
  - name: Example position
    description: Description of the delivered service
    unit_price: 100
    quantity: 1
-- home/.config/invox/template.tex --
Invoice @@INVOICE_NUMBER@@ for @@CUSTOMER_NAME@@
Issued @@ISSUE_DATE@@, due @@DUE_DATE@@
@@LINE_ITEMS_ROWS@@
Subtotal @@SUBTOTAL@@
@@VAT_SUMMARY_ROWS@@
Total @@TOTAL@@
Outstanding @@OUTSTANDING_AMOUNT@@
@@PAYMENT_TERMS_TEXT@@
IBAN @@IBAN@@
